\label{defn:base_change_category}
 Let $F\colon  \scr{A} \to \scr{C}$ be a morphism in $\mathbf{Cat}(\scr{V})$, i.e. a functor of categories enriched in $\scr{V}$. Then there is an $(\scr{A}, \scr{C})$-bimodule $_F \scr{C}$ where the left action of $\scr{A}$ is given by
  \begin{align*}
  \scr{A}(a, a') \otimes ({_F \scr{C}})(a', c) 
   &= \scr{A}(a, a') \otimes \scr{C}(F(a'), c) 
  \\
  &\to \scr{C}(F(a), F(a')) \otimes \scr{C}(F(a'), c) \to \scr{C}(F(a), c) = {_F \scr{C}(a, c)} 
  \end{align*}
  There is a dual $(\scr{C}, \scr{A})$-bimodule that we denote $\scr{C}_F$.

